  "replies": [
    "Sure. Could you share a bit more detail about what you're trying to do? I can give a more specific answer with some context.",
    "Here's a short overview: start with the smallest model that meets your quality bar, measure latency and cost on real traffic, and only move to a larger model if the evaluation results justify it.",
    "I can help with that. The most common cause is a mismatch between the expected input format and what the client is sending. Check the request body and headers first.",
    "Hello! How can I help you today?",
    "That depends on your constraints. If latency matters most, batch smaller requests and enable streaming; if cost matters most, cache repeated prompts and use a smaller model for routing."
  ],
  "changelog": [
    {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "title": "OAuth sign-in and the A2A account assistant",
      "body": "Apps and agents can use OAuth 2.1 (authorization code with PKCE, client credentials, device flow, token exchange) and dynamic client registration. The account assistant now speaks A2A."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "title": "MCP server (beta) and integrations",
      "body": "Manage models, usage and provider keys from MCP clients. Integrations acting for users can register for a higher rate limit."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-26",
      "title": "Public beta",
      "body": "OpenAI-compatible chat and embeddings API for open-weight models, self-serve trial keys, and bring-your-own-key routing to upstream providers and vLLM clusters."
    }
